id: ops-rozk
title: Declare renderer ownership so the host enforces scoping the package only applied at runtime
description: "The renderer overrides self-scoped by checking a private result marker and returning null, which is correct but invisible to the host. Passing the ownership argument makes commands and result ownership enforced before the callback runs."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T21:42:09.635Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T22:14:11.125Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-04T22:14:11.108Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-04T22:14:11.108Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: Both renderer registrations pass a shared ownership object naming the package's own commands and its result discriminator; a test proves the renderer still renders its own marked result and declines a foreign one; coverage stays at 100
resolution: "Renderer ownership enforced by the host before the callback runs; three-axis decline test covers command rejection, result rejection, and both-foreign."
expected_result: A renderer override claims only its own marked results emitted under its own command paths; foreign results and foreign commands fall through to native rendering.
actual_result: "All three decline cases pass for toon and json; dropping the commands array fails the command-rejection case; coverage thresholds met (lines 94.54%, branch 78.68%, funcs 95.44%)."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T21:42:14.727Z",pi-agent,"Derived command paths from the ten api.registerCommand({ name }) calls in index.ts: ops scan (2424), ops policy (2457), ops verify-release (2513), ops report (2582), ops status (2619), ops outdated (2650), ops audit (2680), ops metrics (2710), ops merge-receipts (2785), ops docstrings (2861). All ten commands can return a pmOpsRendered-marked result, either directly via renderedCommandResult() or through the shared emitResult() helper. The resultDiscriminator reuses the extracted isRenderedCommandResult predicate."
close_reason: "Both toon and json registerRenderer calls pass a shared ownership object naming all ten ops command paths plus the isRenderedCommandResult discriminator. The decline test is split into three cases that isolate command rejection (foreign command + marked result) from result rejection (owned command + foreign/bare result), with a belt-and-braces both-foreign case, so the commands declaration is independently covered and cannot be deleted with the suite still green."
body: ""
